  "narrative": "This synthesis resolves the H20 response deadline using the newly delivered independent validation R26. H20 registered TP53 loss as associated with weaker USP7 dependency; because the claim direction is +1, the returned signed positive estimate means the exposed group has a higher, i.e. less negative, USP7 dependency score, corresponding to weaker dependency. Discovery R23 was +0.8019 with 95% Welch interval +0.7823 to +0.8216, n=406 versus 1594. Validation R26 is +0.8041 with independent interval +0.7748 to +0.8334, n=389 versus 1611. The independent interval accounts for the maximum number of validation comparisons in the run. Using the operational 10%-of-absolute-mean threshold for USP7 of about 0.009, both discovery and validation are enormous, roughly eighty times the threshold, and the validation lower bound remains far above null and above clinical irrelevance. The validation estimate is essentially unchanged from discovery. I therefore accept H20 as a robust supplied-dataset association and mark the direct investigation closed because the exact overall TP53-loss versus USP7 dependency comparison is now supported by discovery, internal context tests, and independent validation. This does not close the broader USP7 context program: registered refinements such as library, batch, KRAS-wildtype, KEAP1-intact, SMARCA4-intact, and library-interaction tests remain relevant only as descriptive subgroup or modification questions, not as validation of the main association. The accepted interpretation remains association within the supplied dataset, not proof that TP53 loss causes weaker USP7 dependency or that USP7 targeting should be avoided clinically.\n\nMore broadly, the current strongest supported findings are four internally replicated, very large, dataset-specific dependency associations. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency. The overall effect is +0.7840 (R7); ARID1A-intact context is validated at +0.7846 with independent interval +0.7517 to +0.8174 (H15/R15/R39); batch_a +0.7470, non-Avana +0.8009, TP53-intact +0.7873, KEAP1-intact +0.7833, and KRAS-wildtype +0.7875 are all far above the approximate SMARCA2 threshold of 0.042. This supports SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 as a stable supplied-dataset signal, while leaving causal synthetic-lethality and clinical generalizability unresolved. Second, MSI-high is associated with stronger WRN dependency. Overall +0.7899 is supported by Avana +0.7945, BRCA2-intact +0.7944, TP53-intact +0.7801, KEAP1-intact +0.7871, and STK11-intact +0.7983, all far above the approximate WRN threshold of 0.030. Third, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, opposite the original H8 direction. H8 remains rejected and closed because the signed evidence under its original stronger-dependency direction is negative; the reversed claim H14 is accepted with discovery +0.7961 and independent validation +0.8096, far above the approximate NFE2L2 threshold of 0.009. This signal is also supported in non-Avana, TP53-intact, STK11-intact, and KRAS-wildtype contexts. Fourth, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency, now accepted and direct-validated through H20/R26, with additional large support in non-Avana, SMARCA4-intact, and KEAP1-intact contexts.\n\nThe negative and null-control findings remain informative but are limited to the tested comparisons. The supplied dataset rejects the original KEAP1-loss stronger-NFE2L2 claim H8, KRAS-mutation stronger-STAT3 dependency H2, BRAF V600E stronger-BRAF dependency among KRAS-wildtype samples H5, MYC amplification stronger-DHX9 H10, MYC amplification stronger-RPL11 H11, ARID1A loss stronger-SMARCA2 overall H13, ERBB2 amplification stronger-ERBB2 among KRAS-wildtype samples H27, KRAS mutation weaker-RIT1 dependency H32, research marker D as a clinically meaningful SMARCA2 predictor H59, and PTEN loss weaker-EGFR dependency H73. These reject specific hypotheses in this dataset; they do not establish universal biological absence.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty is concentrated in the driver and technical-context programs. KRAS mutation overall versus stronger KRAS dependency is directionally supportive but imprecise and below robust acceptance: +0.0137, interval -0.0038 to +0.0312. EGFR amplification is borderline overall +0.0252, interval -0.0003 to +0.0507, and in adenocarcinoma or KRAS-wildtype contexts, but these intervals still include null and clinical irrelevance. TP53 loss versus stronger KIF18A dependency narrowly excludes zero at +0.0208, interval +0.0012 to +0.0403, but the point estimate is below the approximate KIF18A threshold and should be treated as hypothesis-generating. NF1 loss versus weaker KRAS dependency is borderline +0.0202, interval -0.0086 to +0.0491; KRAS stratification is needed before stronger inference. Library-interaction tests for SMARCA2/SMARCA4, NFE2L2/KEAP1, and USP7/TP53 are not decisive; the main effects are robust in both library strata, but exact library modification remains uncertain. Technical controls are generally reassuring: marker D is near null for SMARCA2, and matched RNA/DNA omics completeness is near null for SMARCA2, although the upper interval bound for H80 is slightly above threshold, so this remains a weak concern rather than an artifact conclusion.\n\nThe most informative next analyses are the already registered context completions and driver refinements rather than more validation. For accepted signals, finish the descriptive context grid: SMARCA2/SMARCA4 Avana-only and batch_b, ARID1A interaction and ARID1A-loss in SMARCA4-intact cells; USP7/TP53 Avana, batch_a, batch_b, KRAS-wildtype, and library interaction; KEAP1/NFE2L2 batch_a and KEAP1/STK11 interaction; WRN/MSI batch_b. For unresolved driver biology, prioritize subgroup-stratified EGFR/KRAS tests: EGFR amplification in adenocarcinoma KRAS-wildtype cells, KRAS mutation excluding BRAF V600E, ERBB2 amplification effect on EGFR in KRAS-wildtype cells, PIK3CA mutation in KRAS-wildtype KRAS dependency, and KRAS dependency in adenocarcinoma or STK11-intact contexts. If one of these becomes both precise and clinically meaningful, then targeted independent validation would be worthwhile. At present, validation is not needed for the main accepted signals; H20's response deadline has been resolved, and the remaining validation budget is best reserved for a newly sharp borderline driver or specificity result. Overall, the defensible scientific conclusion is that this supplied dataset strongly and internally replicably associates SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, and TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, while several canonical driver and RTK/bypass hypotheses remain negative or unresolved and none of these associations can yet be stated as causal or generalizable.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 4 synthesis update. H20 response deadline resolved: TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency accepted and direct-investigation closed. Evidence: discovery R23 +0.8019 [0.7823,0.8216], validation R26 +0.8041 [0.7748,0.8334], USP7 clinical scale about 0.009; validated and far above threshold. Broad USP7 context claims remain relevant but main overall claim is settled. Current supported dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss/stronger SMARCA2 overall plus ARID1A-intact validated, batch_a, non-Avana, TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, KRAS-wildtype; MSI-high/stronger WRN overall plus Avana, BRCA2-intact, TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, STK11-intact; KEAP1 loss/weaker NFE2L2 reversed from H8 and validated, plus non-Avana, TP53-intact, STK11-intact, KRAS-wildtype; TP53 loss/weaker USP7 overall validated plus non-Avana, SMARCA4-intact, KEAP1-intact. All are association-only. Negative/rejected: H8 original, H2, H5, H10, H11, H13, H27, H32, H59, H73. Unresolved: KRAS mutation overall small/imprecise; EGFR amplification borderline overall and in adeno/KRAS-wt; KIF18A/TP53 borderline; NF1/KRAS borderline and needs KRAS stratification; library/batch interactions for accepted signals not decisive; markers E/F and some technical controls pending. Next analyze priorities: context completion for accepted large signals H16, H39, H21, H31, H35, H36, H42, H37, H65, H22, H40, H47; driver refinements H43, H45, H74, H76, H23, H29, H28/H24 if needed, H30/H33 follow-ups if precise; specificity/controls H69, H78, H79, H81. Validation reserve for new precise clinically meaningful driver or specificity result; no further validation for H20. Do not interpret as causal or generalizable."
